Director General of Police, CID has indicated that he has examined witnesses, that he has collected documentary evidence and that in course of the same he has found -
(1) A case in Cr. No. 26 of 1996 was registered on 4th February, 1996 at about 6 p.m. However, the date was put as 5th February, 1996 and again rubbed off as 4th February, 1996 in the original C.D. file given to us. However, in the Court copy it was shown as 5th February, 1996 only;
(2) In the FIR, the Inspector mentioned that on credible information a deal is going on for the purchase of antiques in a room in Sai Prakash Hotel, he proceeded immediately at 3-15 p.m. on 4th February, 1996. But in the final report, it is mentioned that at about 1400 hrs. on information that some accused involved in Bombay blast case were staying in a room of Sai Prakash Lodge, Shri Jaya Rao visited the lodge and arrested them. (3) As per the seizure list apart from the recovery of the alleged antiques from the house of Shri S. Javeri, it is noticed that the police party also recovered one old fire arm of 1883 vintage and also a full bottle of compagne.
